  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/600606ec-53ad-4fa1-a1b1-a67242e2a4ce-52d8e4b6-8788-47af-a2c6-6e89ec097a11-9894021.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 198px;\" /></p><p>As we know,&nbsp;voltmeter is connected in parallel to the element being measured.</p><p>The equivalent resistance of the above circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Current through the circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>90</mn><mn>180</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Reading of the voltmeter is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>",
